  "classification": {
    "Hash.cpp": "Lengths, algorithm choices and padding positions only; Equal returns one declassified comparison result.",
    "Symmetric.cpp": "AES key size and public rounds; GHASH all indices public; Poly1305 full vs partial block length public; open releases plaintext only after one declassified full tag result.",
    "Curve.cpp": "Fixed scalar bit count and mask selects; exponentiation branch is public exponent; decoding accumulates validity bits without early return; X25519 zero result and final Ed25519 validity are declassified results.",
    "Argon2.cpp": "RFC 9106 \u00a73.4.1.3: direct reference-block access is the sole secret-address exception after pass 0 slices 0\u20131. Phase selection, all branches and loop counts use public parameters; lane/index remainder remains fixed-time. Blake permutations are public; caller memory is wiped. The optional service callback pointer and segment schedule are public; the callback receives only its installed context, no credential or hash-state bytes. Cancellation does not shorten hashing or wiping.",
    "Drbg.cpp": "Input lengths and public reseed counter only; caller-held state changes have no secret-conditioned paths.",
    "Sha256.cpp": "Message length, round number and padding positions are public; kernel HMAC key length is public. The user namespace exposes SHA-256 with volatile workspace wiping.",
    "Internal.hpp": "Unsigned mask, rotate, endian helpers use public word indices and fixed widths; IV constants shared once. Workspace erasure is explicit volatile byte loop. Masks use erased volatile round trips to inhibit secret-conditioned compiler selects.",
    "Crypto.hpp": "Public algorithm enums, explicit buffers, bounded state storage and caller-owned workspace declarations."
  },
